# Deliberate writes to the global environment, for the Check-Repo.ps1 `globals` rule.
# One "<path glob> <name glob>" per line, # comments. KrowiAF*, BINDING_* and SLASH_* names never
# need a line. Everything else the rule finds is an accidental global until it is listed here with
# the reason, so an addition to this file is a review item, not a formality.

# --- addon.OverwriteFunctions (Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua): the FrameXML achievement UI functions the
#     addon replaces on purpose. This is the whole point of the addon; it reshapes AchievementFrame.
#     Blizzard *API* functions (GetAchievementCriteriaInfo, ...) are never allowed here.
#     Not visible to this rule, listed for the review trail: the same file also replaces the table field
#     AchievementTemplateMixin.ProcessClick (same reason as AchievementFrameSummaryAchievement_OnClick below).
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrame_ToggleAchievementFrame
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrame_DisplayComparison
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrame_SelectAchievement
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrame_SetTabs
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrameSummaryAchievement_OnClick    # wrapped: inserts the chat link itself, skipping the protected C_AchievementTelemetry call
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AchievementFrameTab_OnClick
Gui/Gui.lua AchievementFrameTab_OnClick
Gui/WindowFrames/AchievementFrameTabButtonFactory/AchievementFrameTabButtonFactory.lua AchievementFrameTab_OnClick

# --- addon.LoadBlizzardApiChanges (Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua): polyfills for globals Blizzard removed
#     in 10.1.5, defined only when the game no longer provides them (`if not X then X = ... end`)
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua IsTrackedAchievement
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua RemoveTrackedAchievement
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua GetNumTrackedAchievements
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua AddTrackedAchievement
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua MAX_TRACKED_ACHIEVEMENTS
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua WatchFrame_Update
Gui/BlizzardOverrides.lua SetFocusedAchievement

# --- Blizzard frame aliases and constants the classic/retail GUI code adjusts
Gui/Gui.lua AchievementFrameFilterDropdown                                         # alias: the frame is AchievementFrameFilterDropDown on Classic, Filters.FilterDropdown on Retail
Gui/WindowFrames/AchievementFrameHeader.lua AchievementFrameHeaderLeftDDLInset     # named texture other GUI files and skins reach by global name
Gui/WindowFrames/AchievementsObjectives/AchievementsObjectives.lua ACHIEVEMENTBUTTON_METAROWHEIGHT   # Blizzard layout constant, set to 28 on Classic at load
